{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "userdb-hotelling-multiyear-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.61, step 7f. `userdb-hotelling-multiyear`: Total Energy (91) at running exhaust, extended idle and APU for the passenger car and the combination long-haul truck in Washtenaw County, DEFAULT domain, 2015 AND 2020, April and August, both day types, hours 7 and 8, from the default database plus a USER INPUT DATABASE (`<databaseselections>`) stating the six idle and hotelling ADJUSTMENT tables -- `scale-county-idle-adjust`'s database with every year-keyed table at both years (`inputs/washtenaw-userdb-hotelling-multiyear.esm`). A county domain database may hold one year only (MOVES refuses two), so this is how those tables reach a multi-year run. MOVESOutput is 15,616 rows.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is what AdjustHotelling.sql does at a SECOND year. TotalActivityGenerator clears hotellingHours only when the process changes, so when it adjusts 2020 the table still holds 2015's rows, already adjusted and cut to the run's hours; the hour, age and month blocks take their default shares over every row the table holds and rewrite every row. Measured in pandas from the execution database before the port: a replay of the four blocks over 2015's rows and 2020's TAG hours reproduces 2020's 984 `hotellingHours` rows at 4.2e-15 and the age block's own leftover table (`newHotellingHours_had`, both years) at 4.3e-15, where adjusting 2020 alone misses by up to 52% (median 38%). 2015, the first year, is the one-year computation (PLAN.md §7.3.61).\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to 1952, the (pollutant-process, cohort) pairs per (county, month, hour-day) cell over both years, recomputed as `rateSurvivorCount`.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "idle-adjustment",
      "hotelling-adjustment",
      "user-input-database",
      "multi-year"
    ]
  },
